\name{cellucid_annotation_publish}
\alias{cellucid_annotation_publish}
\title{Vote and suggest labels}
\usage{
cellucid_annotation_publish(viewer, suggestions, votes)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{suggestions}{The new labels, each for one category; one label once per category. A vector or list of a named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{votes}{The votes, each on one suggestion of one category; one vote per suggestion. A vector or list of a named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{not_published} (The person's other changes still not published (null when not known)), \code{published} (Where the changes went, as one commit: written to the repository, in a pull request its authors merge, or nowhere (the votes were already so)), \code{pull_request} (The pull request, when they went to one), \code{repository} (The GitHub repository of the community annotation), \code{suggestions} (Each suggestion, in the order given), \code{votes} (Each vote, in the order given, with its suggestion's counts now).
}
\description{
Vote suggested labels of categories up or down (none takes the person's vote back) and suggest new labels in the person's name (each with their upvote, as the voting dialog's New suggestion does), and publish all of them together as one commit: the person's own file in the community annotation repository is written as published now plus these changes (a pull request when they cannot write to the repository), which others see on their next Pull. Put everything of a turn in one call: each call is one commit of the person's file and one question to them. Nothing else of the person's is published; votes that change nothing publish nothing. A label already suggested for its category is refused with its id (vote on it instead), and nothing of a call is published when any of it is refused. Asked of the person first; the history cannot take it back. Refused until the person has connected the repository and signed in to GitHub.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{annotation.publish} (Community annotation). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

It publishes for others to see, so the viewer asks the person first (publishes), from R too, as when an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it; \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} waits for their answer (call it again if its timeout passes first).
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_annotation_publish(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
